                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Purchase Date: [/h1]\n19th of October 2020 - 19/10/2020\n\n[h1] Purchase Value: [/h1]\n1.50€\n\n\n[h1] PROS & CONS Review: [/h1]\nPROS:\n+ Easy to learn and play.\n+ Short game sessions.\n+ Educational.\n+ Easy to 100% Steam achievements.\n\nCONS:\nNo information available.\n\n\n[h1] Text Review: [/h1]\nMajotori is an intriguing cultural trivia video game where choices matter.\nIt's easy to learn and play.\nIt's good for people who have only from ten to thirty minutes available to play.\nIt's indirectly educational for those who care about the culture of video games, movies, and anime.\nI didn't notice any negative aspects while playing.\nThis paragraph is for the achievement hunters. It's easy to obtain 100% of the Steam achievements, as it's just a matter of trying out different possibilities, and memorizing some answers. You can also use one of the many Steam guides available. Additionally, there are no tasks that require grinding.\n\n\n[h1] Recommendation: [/h1]\nIt's an interesting little game, and for the price I paid, I don't regret it.\nI recommend it.\n\n\n[h1] Rating - 70/100 [/h1]\nReview Date - 01/11/2026",
